      "problem": "Factor ${t}^{2}-22t+121.$",
      "worked_solution": "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}-2at+{a}^{2}=(t-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}-22t+121.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-22t+{11}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-2\\cdot 11t+{11}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=11.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-11)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
